# Verification

These rules apply before an AI agent reports any work as finished.

- Run the checks the repository already provides — its test suite, linter,
  formatter, and pre-commit hooks — and name the ones that were run.
- Size the test run to the moment. A whole suite takes minutes and its output
  fills the context, so it is not the check to repeat after every edit:
  - while editing, run the one test file, or the one test, of the code in
    hand;
  - before reporting, run the tests covering everything that changed: with
    the repository's own selector when it has one (`--changed`, `--related`,
    `--affected`), otherwise the test files of every module touched;
  - run the whole suite once, before a merge or a push, when the change
    reaches what every test shares, or when no smaller set can be named.
    Never rerun it over a tree it already passed on, and never for a change
    to documentation alone.
- Say which of these ran. A selected run is a verified change; it is not "the
  whole suite passes", so do not report it as that.
- Ask a test runner for its failures only (a quiet or summary mode) rather
  than reading every passing line.
- Never bypass a check to make a commit land: no `--no-verify`, no skipping
  hooks, and no disabling a lint rule to silence a warning instead of fixing
  the code behind it.
- Report results faithfully. If a test fails, say so and include the relevant
  output. If a check was skipped or could not run, say that too, and why.
- "It should work" is not verification. Either a check ran, or the work is
  reported as unverified.
- When something cannot be verified automatically, state exactly what the user
  has to do to confirm it.
- A change on a security path (credentials handling, permissions, hooks,
  anything under `secrets/`) is reviewed by a fresh subagent that did not
  write it. A security fix counts as proven only when reverting it makes its
  test fail.
- Finish the whole task before reporting. If part of it is blocked, complete
  everything else and say plainly what was left out and why.
